Version 0.92.0 (2026-09-14)
* NEW FEATURE: Detect and properly warn about Cloudflare and Anubis challenge protections.
* NEW FEATURE: Produce MacOS build artifacts (package)
* CHANGE: Store Windows INI settings in the roaming profile
* CHANGE: Silently skip notification sounds when no audio backend is available
* CHANGE: Enforce TLS certificate validation. Remove the SSL modal dialog for SSL exceptions. Report any issues with SSL certificates.
* BUG FIX: Hopefully a fix for a class of SQLite errors that resulted in the app crashing.
* BUG FIX: Fix Settings page unecessary scrolling
* BUG FIX: Fix RTL article alignment in QTextDocument
* BUG FIX: Fix RTL article list without mirroring the entire view

Version 0.91.0 (2026-09-12)

* NEW FEATURE: Check GitHub Releases for updates and display release notes.
* NEW FEATURE: Add configurable scheduled, exit, subscription and pre-upgrade backups, including database snapshots and settings copies, retention and optional starred-or-labelled-only snapshots.
* NEW FEATURE: Show persistent feed-error details and animated warning indicators; clear warnings after successful retrieval and hide them for disabled feeds.
* NEW FEATURE: Discover application styles and translations at runtime, with external style and language metadata.
* NEW FEATURE: Add independent console/file logging controls, command-line help and log-location opening.
* CHANGED: Rebrand as NotQuiteRSS and centralize application identity, version, URLs and paths in project.json.
* CHANGED: Use new configuration, data and resource paths without automatic migration; existing users must copy their data and settings manually.
* CHANGED: Centralize assets under resources/ and unify Linux, Windows and macOS resource deployment, including Windows package verification.
* CHANGED: Add FLAC, MP3 and All Files options to notification sound pickers.
* CHANGED: Remove the legacy About History tab and bundled QuiteRSS histories; link to Releases and the original project from About.
* CHANGED: Keep only NotQuiteRSS release notes in CHANGELOG.
* BUG FIX: Correct settings access during database preparation and simplify backup completion feedback with a Show button.
* BUG FIX: Correct Windows application-style deployment.

Version 0.90.2 (2026-09-10)

* CHANGED: Multiple behind-the-scenes improvements (part 1) - may result in new bugs :-(
* CHANGED: Restore custom external browser support and log opened resources to the console
* NEW FEATURE: Add full Qt6 support (now the default for Windows CI)
* NEW FEATURE: Drop QtMultimedia dependency and switch to miniaudio

Version 0.90.1 (2026-09-08)

* Fix unwanted in-memory database saves when moving to the tray.
* Fix application menu behavior based on the news article state.
* Fix unbounded cleanup history with publication-age retention; the feeds database (feeds.db) is now properly cleaned up on exit and respects your article retention settings.

Version 0.90.0 (2026-09-06)

* Transforms into a pure Qt5 application.
* Removes browser behavior, browser tabs/navigation/preferences and ad blocking.
* Replaces `QtWebKit` with `QTextBrowser`/`QTextDocument` (articles can still be read in the app!).
* Articles display sanitized feed-provided content; web links open externally.
* Retains reader tabs, newspaper mode, search within articles, selection/copy, zoom, printing/export, and article actions.
* Implements controlled image fetching, TLS certificate verification, supported-format negotiation and optional image diagnostics.
* Requires the installed Qt5 `QtSingleApplication` instead of the bundled copy.
* Updates Linux CI to use a Fedora 44 container and packaged dependencies.
* Updates Windows CI to actually work.
* Removes the bundled `3rdparty/qtsingleapplication` directory.
* Drops the `3rdparty/sqlite` directory, without changing its build rules.
* Fixes Windows and macOS builds (now that we've dropped built-in SQLite).
* Removes FTP support and drops `3rdparty/qftp`.
* Replaces `QzRegExp` uses with `QRegularExpression`/`QRegularExpressionMatch`, and drops `3rdparty/qupzilla`.
* Applies certain functional patches made after QuiteRSS version 0.19.4.
* Sharing methods are now dynamic and moved to an INI file, `social-networks.ini`.
* Adds Link Time Optimization (LTO) by default for all targets.
* Fixes all compilation warnings.
